<h2>Questions from St. Paul property owners</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Is ice dam damage covered in Minnesota?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Many policies cover sudden water damage from ice dams, while excluding long-term seepage or the ice itself. The wording varies, so read your policy carefully. Appraisal can resolve the amount once coverage is accepted.</p></div></details><details><summary>My insurer priced my slate roof as asphalt. What can I do?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Ask for the basis of the estimate in writing, document the existing material, and get a qualified slate contractor’s opinion. If the carrier still won’t move, appraisal is one way to contest the amount.</p></div></details><details><summary>Do you work on Summit Avenue and other historic homes?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Yes. We regularly price older homes and account for materials and methods that match the original construction.</p></div></details></div>
